Modified upstream files (all other copied files remain unchanged):
src/server_api.rs
  Add DispatchOutcome and dispatch_all_clients_with_budget(data, max_requests,
  max_duration, client_quantum). Result type can be inferred by callers through
  wayland-server Display::backend(), without a new direct dependency.
src/rs/server_impl/common_poll.rs
  Check count/time/quantum before each request, including display/registry paths.
  Retain serial-qualified client IDs in a deduplicated round-robin queue across
  calls; sample only one nonblocking readiness batch between quanta. Keep legacy
  APIs unbounded and able to drain retained clients. Treat interrupted readiness
  samples as empty instead of hiding the pending queue behind an error result.
src/rs/server_impl/handle.rs
  Explicitly deregister dead clients before dropping their original socket FDs,
  including handler-initiated kills at budget boundaries. This prevents retained
  socket duplicates from keeping stale Linux epoll registrations alive.
src/sys/server_impl/mod.rs
  Return io::ErrorKind::Unsupported without dispatch on the bounded API.

Added vendored file: PATCHES (this file).
Repository integration files: Cargo.toml ([patch.crates-io] only), Cargo.lock
(remove only the registry source/checksum of wayland-backend), and new real
socket integration tests in tests/backend_fairness.rs. No dependency upgrade.

Caller contract: schedule an explicit continuation wake on more_pending; it can
be conservative at a budget boundary, so stop wakes when a turn returns false.
No idle polling and no reliance on FD readability for userspace-buffered input.
Zero count, duration, or quantum consumes no requests. Time is cooperative:
no hard preemption of a request/visibility/bind handler, parsing, destructor,
cleanup, or scheduler overhead is promised. Only dispatched requests are counted.
